  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two strings, SSS and TTT, of lengths NNN and MMM respectively.\n\nYou can perform the following operation **on the string SSS**:\n\n\nReplace a substring with its first character. (i.e. “ab**cab**c” -&gt; “ab**c**c”)\nWhat is the minimum number of operations to make both of the strings equal? Or determine that it is impossible to make both of the strings equal.\n\n\nInput Format\n\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of testcases.\n\n\n\n\nThe first line of each testcase consists of two space-separated integers NNN and MMM denoting the lengths of the strings SSS and TTT, respectively.\n\n\n\n\nThe second line of each testcase contains the string SSS of length NNN.\n\n\n\n\nThe third line of each testcase contains the string TTT of length MMM.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, output a single line containing a single integer denoting the minimum number of operations to make the strings equal, or −1-1−1 if it is not possible to do so.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\le T \\le 10^31≤T≤103",
      "1≤N,M≤2⋅1031 \\le N, M \\le 2 \\cdot 10^31≤N,M≤2⋅103",
      "Both strings SSS and TTT consists of lowercase English alphabets only.",
      "The sum of NNN over all testcases won't exceed 2⋅1032 \\cdot 10^32⋅103.",
      "The sum of MMM over all testcases won't exceed 2⋅1032 \\cdot 10^32⋅103."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4 3\naabc\naab\n8 8\naccepted\naccapted\n1 1\nz\nz",
        "output": "1\n-1\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTestcase 111:\n\nYou can make SSS equal to TTT using one operation on SSS: \"aabc\" -> \"aab\"\n\nTestcase 222:\n\nIt is impossible to make SSS equal to TTT using the operation.\n\nTestcase 333:\n\nBoth strings are already equal."
      }
    ]
  },
